            "Basic mode learns molecular factors from pixel-level m/z intensity profiles. Spatially Regularized mode additionally encourages neighboring pixels "
            "to have similar molecular-factor weights during model refinement, producing more spatially coherent domains. Co-Clustering / m/z Module mode also "
            "groups m/z features by shared spatial behavior, linking molecular feature modules to discovered cell or tissue regions. Discovered domains can be "
            "thresholded, edited, labeled, and exported as ROIs or masks for downstream analysis. This workflow is inspired by segmentation-free spatial-omics ideas "
            "and MSI spatial co-clustering concepts, but it is not FICTURE or TRIFASE."
